# These are Google OAuth credentials for an installed ("Desktop app") client.
# They are NOT confidential: RFC 8252 classifies a native app as a public
# client, and anything compiled into the binary can be read back out of it.
# What protects the sign-in is PKCE, the loopback redirect, and the fact that
# the only scope requested is drive.appdata — a folder the app creates and
# nothing else in your Drive.
#
# They are kept out of the repository so they stay out of git history and out
# of the way of secret scanners, not because keeping them would make them safe.
#
# Without this file the app builds and runs exactly as before; the Google Drive
# option simply is not offered. Make your own at console.cloud.google.com:
#   1. enable the Google Drive API
#   2. Google Auth Platform → Data Access → add .../auth/drive.appdata
#   3. Audience → Publish app  (in Testing, refresh tokens die after 7 days)
#   4. Clients → Create client → Desktop app

REUP_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
REUP_GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=
